# ADR-031 rule 1: default yubiOS images ship virtio-gpu only. ADR-031 settled
# the *mechanism* (modprobe blacklist + dracut omit + tmpfiles remove); the
# devtmpfs daemon that mounts /dev at boot still re-creates /dev/vfio as a
# structural kernel object (the vfio subsystem registers itself regardless of
# whether any module is loaded). The OMN-149 diagnostic at commit 2a0d5e58
# confirmed: systemd-tmpfiles-setup ran cleanly at 10:07:10 with `Finished`,
# no vfio modules loaded, yet /dev/vfio was recreated at 10:08 (~1 min later)
# before the test asserted. The kernel cdev (10,196) is harmless without the
# module behind it, but its mere existence is the exact attack-surface
# signal tests/vm/test-vgpu-virtio-ci.sh's `test ! -e /dev/vfio` assertion
# is checking.
#
# Udev sees every device node that devtmpfs creates (the kernel fires an
# `add` uevent). RUN+=/bin/rm in this rule removes /dev/vfio the moment
# udev processes the event, so devtmpfs races against an immediate
# delete instead of leaving the node in place until the next tmpfiles pass.
# Belt-and-suspenders with yubiOS-no-vfio-purge.service (catches anything
# udev misses, e.g. a hotplug while the test is running).
#
# See refs/vgpu-vfio-user-trust-boundary-2026-07-25.md.
KERNEL=="vfio", RUN+="/bin/rm -rf /dev/vfio /dev/vfio/*"
KERNEL=="vfio*", RUN+="/bin/rm -f /dev/%k"

